# BMW i3 five-door electric hatchback, 2013-2022.
#
# The first purpose-built BMW electric car: the carbon-fibre passenger cell,
# the aluminium chassis, the tall narrow body, the full-glass tailgate and
# the blue highlight trim. The Range Extender is the same body and is not
# separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_i3_(hatchback)
#
# Dimensions 3.999 x 1.775 x 1.578 m, wheelbase 2.570 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show a UK car in side, front and rear
# views; the side view governs the tall body and the flat tail.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the BMW (UK) i3 price list valid from January 2014:
# Capparis White, Arravani Grey, Andesit Silver and Laurus Grey, all with the
# BMW i Blue highlight. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 150 km/h (electronically limited). Comfort 75/443, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 75: a quiet, upright electric cabin. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 2013 intro, retires staggered 2038-2041.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-i3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-i3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-i3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear side-glass drop is too subtle, and the hatch
# graphic and rear lamps are simplified. The rear-hinged coach doors are shown
# closed. At 128 px the tall body, flat tail, i Blue highlights and black roof
# read as an i3.


